## Context

Neither maw-audit (mutation axes) nor test-audit-llm (read-and-judge
lenses) checks whether an output value is data-derived or memorized. The
paper's hardcoding audit (arXiv:2604.21965 App. B.4) flags a numeric
literal asserted or returned with no computation path from data — the
"toothless test that hardcodes its expected value" failure mode, detected
mechanically.

## Actions

1. Prototype an AST-based detector (Python `ast`): numeric literal in an
   assert/return with no data-derived expression upstream in the function.
2. Decide the home — a test-audit-llm lens vs a maw-audit pre-pass; prefer
   mechanical-first per the harness invariant; document the choice.
3. Known-bad fixture (hardcoded expected value, no computation) as anchor.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Detector implemented, AST-first, LLM only for ambiguous data flow
- [ ] Wired into the chosen skill and documented
- [ ] Fixture catches the hardcoded-value case (RED pre-fix)
